WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.752
Part three: reading the dive profile chart.

00:00:03.902 --> 00:00:09.605
These buttons switch the chart's view. We stay on Profile, in full screen.

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:16.208
Time runs left to right in minutes; depth runs down in metres, with the surface at zero.

00:00:16.358 --> 00:00:25.112
The blue line is you: down at 20 m/min to 40 m, and 20 min of bottom time, the yellow bracket.

00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:33.940
The red dashed curve is the ceiling: the shallowest depth allowed right now. At the end of the bottom time it is almost 17 m.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:43.842
So no direct ascent: the shaded band is off limits. Ascend to 21 m and switch to EAN50 at the purple dot.

00:00:43.992 --> 00:00:51.220
Then the stops, a staircase every 3 m, each deeper than the ceiling while your tissues off-gas.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:59.426
The ceiling rises to the surface; you surface at 39 min, the total dive time (TDT).

00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:06.179
The green dotted line is the average depth, 24.1 m, used for gas planning.

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:14.380
The ceiling line is a guide for your current depth; the planner puts stops on a 3 m grid, a little deeper.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:18.963
Next: the pressure–pressure diagram. Thanks for watching!
